    <main className="not-found tab-enter">
      <BananaMark size={56} />
      <p className="eyebrow">Error 404</p>
      <h1>This page slipped away</h1>
      <p>We couldn&apos;t find what you were looking for. The link may be old or the address may have a typo.</p>
      <Link href="/" className="primary-button">
        Back to home
      </Link>
    </main>
  );
}
```
Check `node_modules/next/dist/docs/01-app/03-api-reference/03-file-conventions/not-found.md` whether `not-found.tsx` supports a `metadata` export; if yes, add `export const metadata: Metadata = { title: 'Page not found · Banana Bank' };` (import type Metadata from 'next'). If unsupported/unclear, skip it.

2. `app/styles/not-found.css` (new), and add `@import './styles/not-found.css';` to `app/globals.css` after the `documents.css` line (before `responsive.css`). Use only existing tokens (see `app/styles/tokens.css`), no new hex colors:
```css
.not-found {
  min-height: 100dvh;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  text-align: center;
  padding: 40px 24px;
}
.not-found .banana-mark-icon {
  color: var(--forest);
  margin-bottom: 22px;
}
.not-found h1 {
  margin-bottom: 10px;
}
.not-found p:not(.eyebrow) {
  max-width: 38ch;
  margin-bottom: 26px;
}
```
First check how `.banana-mark-icon` is styled elsewhere (grep in app/styles, e.g. sidebar.css/motion.css) — if it already sets `display:inline-flex`/color via a parent, adapt so the mark renders in brand green (`var(--forest)`) and centered. `.eyebrow`, `h1`, `.primary-button` already exist in `app/styles/base.css`; reuse them, don't redefine.

## Verify
- `npm run typecheck` and `npx prettier --check app/not-found.tsx app/styles/not-found.css app/globals.css` (fix formatting with `--write` if needed; prettier config: singleQuote, printWidth 100, trailingComma all).
- Dev server: one may already be running on :3000/:4001 from earlier sessions — check with `lsof -ti :3000` and reuse; otherwise start `npm run dev` in background (timeout 0). Leave it running at the end.
- `curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' http://127.0.0.1:3000/this-does-not-exist` must print `404`, and `curl -s http://127.0.0.1:3000/` should still be 200. Also confirm `curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/does-not-exist` still behaves as before (just report the code; the API catch-all at app/api/[...path]/route.ts is unrelated and must not change).
- Playwright screenshot evidence: create `submission/tools/capture-not-found.mjs` modelled on `submission/tools/capture-chat-polish.mjs` (same imports/BASE/usage pattern, `<out-dir>` arg). It should visit `/this-does-not-exist` at 1440x900 and at 390x844 (mobile), wait for networkidle, screenshot full page as `not-found-desktop.png` / `not-found-mobile.png`, and assert that `a.primary-button[href="/"]` exists and that clicking it navigates to `/` (URL ends with `/` and `.app-shell` becomes visible). Run it with out dir `submission/evidencias/despues/25-not-found` (run from submission/tools where playwright is installed in its node_modules). Report the screenshot paths.
- Do not run the full test suite.

Report: final diff (`git diff -- app/ submission/tools/capture-not-found.mjs` plus `git status --short app submission`), command outputs, and screenshot paths. If the dev server throws any warning related to not-found, include it verbatim.

